statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ, U, N ⊆ ℝ^P, R = (M, θ, ξ) an IMRep U n, y₀ ∈ ℝ^P, r, β ∈ ℝ with β ≥ 0 and B_{3r}(y₀) ⊆ U, and Pt : ℝ^P → L(ℝ^P, ℝ^P). Assume:
- Pt is C¹ on B_{3r}(y₀), and Pt(y) is self-adjoint for y ∈ B_{3r}(y₀);
- ‖DPt(y)‖ ≤ β for y ∈ B_{2r}(y₀);
- for q ∈ N ∩ B_{3r}(y₀), Pt(q) maps ℝ^P into T_qN = tangentSpace N q and fixes T_qN pointwise;
- μ_R-a.e. x lies in N;
- for μ_R-a.e. x ∈ B_{3r}(y₀), approxTangentPlane n M x ⊆ T_xN;
- x ↦ p_x (orthogonal projection onto approxTangentPlane n M x) is μ_R-AEMeasurable;
- V = v(M, θ) is stationary in U ∩ N (R.IsStationaryAlong N).
Then there is a μ_R-a.e. strongly measurable H : ℝ^P → ℝ^P with |H(x)| ≤ nβ for all x and δV(X) = −∫⟨X, H⟩ dμ_R for every C¹ vector field X with compact support contained in B_{2r}(y₀).
